# Aurelia's Vindicator (4/2 flying, lifelink, ward {2}; Disguise {X}{3}{W}): "When this creature is turned face up, exile up to X other target creatures from the
# battlefield and/or creature cards from graveyards. When this creature leaves the battlefield, return the exiled cards to their owners' hands." (CR 702.168d-e, 107.3d,
# 607.2a). Bot1 casts it face down with a Black Lotus on turn 1; on turn 3 it Bolts one of Bot2's two Memnites. On turn 5 it turns the Vindicator up with X = 2, paying
# {2}{3}{W} (six Moxen, the pool empty after): two targets may be chosen, the Vindicator itself and a Mox are refused, and the Memnite in Bot2's graveyard and the one on its
# battlefield are exiled. On turn 6 Bot2 Bolts the Vindicator (4/2): both Memnites go to Bot2's hand, their owner's, the Memnite on the battlefield and the card from the
# graveyard alike.

